--TEST--
`Core\Command::run` refuses an enum argument written as ADR 0010 § 3's backing value, which is the other side of the case name being the spelling — ADR 0086 § 6
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The bound asserted from the side that a conversion accepting *both* would
// pass: `command-run-converts-an-enum-argument-by-its-case-name` shows the word
// `Error` reaching the handler as 20, and a reading that also admitted the
// digits would answer that case identically while quietly giving a command line
// two spellings for one case. A backing value is storage — an author may
// renumber it without touching a name — so it is not something a person types.
//
// `run` prints its usage page to standard error, which a case does not read, so
// the refusal is asserted as § 6's usage status and by the handler never
// running: a converted `10` would have printed a line before `run` returned.
enum Level: uint {
    Warn = 10,
    Error = 20,
}

class Logs {
    #[Core\Command(name: "emit", about: "Write one line at a level")]
    public static function emit(Level $level): uint {
        echo "level: ", $level as uint, "\n";
        return 0;
    }
}

echo "status: ", Core\Command::run(), "\n";
--ARGS--
emit
10
--EXPECT--
status: 2
